<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Recceswinth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 649–672</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Recceswinth was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 649 to 672, first as co-ruler with his father Chindasuinth and alone from 653. In 654 he issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigothic-code">Liber Iudiciorum</a>, the Visigothic Code, a single law for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> and Hispano-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> alike that remained influential in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> for centuries. One of the votive crowns of the Treasure of Guarrazar bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/recceswinth.jpg" alt="Recceswinth" width="320" height="667" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ángel M. Felicísimo from Mérida, España · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corona_de_(29049230050).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
